{"r":"nfx","lane":{"p":2821,"e":[{"h":"نَفَخَ بِفَمِهِ","t":["(K,) aor. , [accord, to Golius and Freytag, incorrectly, ; see Kur, iii. 43, &c.] inf. n. ",[2,"نَفْخٌ"],"; (Msb;) and ↓ ",[2,"نفّخ"],", (K,) inf. n. ",[2,"تَنْفِيخٌ"],"; (TA;) ",[1,"He blew with his mouth; sent forth wind from his mouth;"]," (K;) this is done in taking rest, and in labour or exertion, and the like. (L.) ",[2,"نَفَخَ"]," is mostly used as a neut. v.; but sometimes it is trans., as many have asserted: you say ",[2,"نَفَخَ الصُّورَ"],", as well as ",[2,"نَفَخَ فِيهِ"],", ",[1,"He blew the trumpet,"]," or ",[1,"blew into the trumpet:"]," (MF, TA:) ",[2,"نَفَخَهُ"]," is a dial. form of ",[2,"نَفَخَ فِيهِ"],": (S:) also, ",[2,"نَفَخَ"],[2,"فِى النَّارِ"]," [",[1,"he blew the fire;"]," or ",[1,"blew into the fire"],"]: [see 8 (last sentence) in art. ",[2,"قوت"],":] and ",[2,"نَفَخَ فى"],[2,"الزِّقِّ"]," [",[1,"he blew into,"]," or ",[1,"inflated, the skin"],"]: and sometimes one says ",[2,"نَفَخَهُ"],". (Msb.) ",[2,"نُفْخُوا"]," occurs in a verse of El-Katámee for ",[2,"نُفِخُوا"],". (S.) ― -b2- ",[2,"نَفَخَ الشَّيْطَانُ فِى أَنْفِهِ"]," (assumed tropical:) [",[1,"The devil blew into his nose"],"]: said of him who aspires to that which is not for him. (TA.) ― -b3- ",[2,"نَفَخَ شِدْقَيْهِ"]," (tropical:) [",[1,"He inflated,"]," or ",[1,"puffed out, the sides of his mouth;"]," meaning] ",[1,"he was proud,"]," or ",[1,"affected pride."]," (A.) ― -b4- ",[2,"نَفَخَهُ"],", aor. , inf. n. ",[2,"نَفْخٌ"],", ",[1,"It"]," (food) ",[1,"inflated him,"]," or ",[1,"filled him."]," (L.) ― -b5- ",[2,"نَفِخَ"],", aor. , inf. n. (L) ",[2,"نَفَخٌ"],", (S, L,) ",[1,"He"]," (a man, S, and a horse, L) ",[1,"had inflated testicles."]," (S, L.) ― -b6- Also, ",[1,"He"]," (a beast of carriage) ",[1,"had his pasterns inflated with wind."]," When a beast thus affected walks, the humour subsides. (L.) ― -b7- ",[2,"نَفَخَ نِهَا"],[1,"Pepedit; crepitum ventris emisit."]," (S, K.) ― -b8- ",[2,"نَفَخَتِ الرِّيحُ"],[1,"The wind came suddenly."]," (L.) ― -b9- ",[2,"نَفَخَتْ بِهِمُ"],[2,"الطَّرِيقُ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"The road cast"]," [or ",[1,"brought"],"] ",[1,"them suddenly"]," [to a place]: from ",[2,"نفخت الريح"],". (L.) -A2- ",[2,"نَفَخَتِ"],[2,"الضُّحَى"],", inf. n. ",[2,"نَفْخٌ"],", (tropical:) ",[1,"The morning became advanced, and the sun high."]," (L, K.) You say also ",[2,"النَّهَارُ"]," ↓ ",[2,"انتفخ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"The day became advanced, the sun being high,"]," (S, L,) ",[1,"an hour before noon."]," (L.)"],"f":"1"},{"h":"نَفَّخَ","t":["see 1."],"f":"2"},{"h":"تَنَفَّخَ","t":["see 8."],"f":"5"},{"h":"انتفخ","t":[[1,"It"]," (a thing, S, as a skin, Msb,) ",[1,"became inflated,"]," or ",[1,"puffy;"]," (S, A, Msb;) as also ↓ ",[2,"تنفّخ"],": (A:) also, ",[1,"it became swollen; i. q."],[2,"وَرِمَ"],". (K, art. ",[2,"ورم"],".) ― -b2- ",[2,"انتفخ"],[1,"He became inflated,"]," or ",[1,"filled,"]," by food. (L.) See 1. ― -b3- ",[2,"إِنْتِفَاخُ الأَهِلَّةِ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"The bigness"]," [or ",[1,"swelling"],"] ",[1,"of the new moons."]," Occurring in a trad. respecting the signs of the last day. (L.) [See ",[2,"انتفج"],".] ― -b4- ",[2,"انتفخ عَلَىَّ"]," (assumed tropical:) [",[1,"He became inflated against me;"]," i. e.] ",[1,"he was angry with me."]," (TA.) And ",[2,"انتفخ لَهُ"]," (assumed tropical:) [",[1,"He behaved angrily to him"],"]. (TA in art. ",[2,"زحر"],".)"],"f":"8"},{"h":"نَفْخٌ","t":["[",[1,"Flatulence."]," ― -b2- And hence,] (tropical:) ",[1,"Boastfulness; arrogance; pride;"]," (S, K;) [",[1,"inflation with pride"],"]: pride was termed by Mohammad ",[2,"نَفْخُ الشَّيْطَانِ"],". (TA, art. ",[2,"همز"],".) ― -b3- ",[2,"رَجُلٌ ذُو نَفْخٍ"],", as also ",[2,"ذو"],[2,"نَفْجِ"],", (tropical:) ",[1,"A boastful, arrogant, proud man;"]," (S;) [",[1,"a man inflated with pride"],"]."]},{"h":"نُفُخٌ","t":["(assumed tropical:) A young man (TA) ",[1,"full of youthfulness"]," [or ",[1,"youthful plumpness"]," or ",[1,"vigour"],"]; (K;) and so, without ",[2,"ة"],", a damsel. (TA.)"]},{"h":"نَفْخَةٌ","t":["and ",[2,"نُفْخَةٌ"]," and ",[2,"نِفْخَةٌ"],[1,"Inflation of the belly"]," (S, K) by food &c. (TA.) You say ",[2,"بِهِ"],[2,"نفخةٌ"],[1,"He has an inflation of the body:"]," (K:) and ",[2,"أَجِدُ نفخةً"],[1,"I experience an inflation of the body."]," (S.) ― -b2- [And ",[1,"A flatulent humour"]," of any kind: a meaning well known.] ― -b3- ",[2,"النَّفْخَةُ"],[1,"The blast"]," [",[1,"of the horn"],"] ",[1,"of the day of resurrection."]," (L.) ― -b4- ",[2,"نَفْخَةٌ"],[1,"A slight odour:"]," differing from ",[2,"نَفْحَةٌ"],", which is a plenteous odour. (L.) ― -b5- ",[2,"نَفْخَةُ الشَّبَابِ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"The chief part of youth."]," (L.) ",[2,"نَفْخَةُ الرَّبِيعِ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"The time of the season called"],[2,"الربيع"],[1,"when the earth produces herbs,"]," or ",[1,"herbage:"]," (A:) or ",[2,"نُفْخَةُ الربيع"],", and ",[2,"نِفْخَتُهُ"],", ",[1,"the time of that season when vegetation has ended."]," (AZ:) ― -b6- ",[2,"نُفْخَةٌ"],[1,"A disease that attacks a horse, and makes his testicles to swell."]," (L.) ― -b7- See ",[2,"نُفَّاخٌ"],"."]},{"h":"نَفْخَآءُ","t":["(applied to land, or ground, S) ",[1,"i. q."],[2,"نَبْخَآءُ"],": (S, L, K:) or ",[1,"elevated and good"]," or ",[1,"fertile ground, in which is no sand nor stones, producing a few trees;"]," and so ",[2,"نَهْدَآءُ"],", except that this latter is more flat and extensive: or ",[1,"soft land, in which is elevation:"]," (L:) or ",[1,"tumid earth, that breaks in pieces when trodden upon:"]," (TA, voce ",[2,"رَخَّآءُ"],":) pl. ",[2,"نَفَاخِىُّ"],": it has a form of pl. proper to substs, because it is an epithet in which the quality of a subst. predominates. (L.) ― -b2- ",[2,"نَفْخَآءُ"]," The ",[1,"upper part of the bone of the"],[2,"ساق"]," [or ",[1,"shank,"]," or ",[1,"tibia"],"]. (K.)"]},{"h":"نَفِيخٌ","t":["One ",[1,"who is employed to blow a fire."]," (K.)"]},{"h":"نُفَّاخٌ","t":[[1,"An inflation of a humour occasioned by disease,"]," (T, K,) ",[1,"arising in any part:"]," (T:) ",[1,"a humour;"]," as also ↓ ",[2,"نَفْخَةٌ"],". (L.) ― -b2- See ",[2,"نُفَّاخَةٌ"],"."]},{"h":"نُفَّاخَةٌ","t":[[1,"A bubble"]," upon water. (L, K [but in some copies of the K, for ",[2,"الحَجَاةُ"]," is erroneously put ",[2,"الحجارة"],".]) ― -b2- [The ",[1,"air-bladder of a fish;"],"] ",[1,"an inflated thing in the belly of a fish, which is"]," (",[1,"as they assert,"]," L,) ",[1,"its"],[2,"نِصَاب"]," [app. meaning its ",[1,"most essential part,"]," or ",[1,"element,"],"] ",[1,"by means of which it rises in the water, and moves to and fro."]," (L, K.) ― -b3- ",[1,"A bladder of a plant"]," (S, O, L, voce ",[2,"قَتَادٌ"],", &c.) N. un. of ",[2,"نُفَّاخٌ"]," (AHn, in TA, voce ",[2,"عُشَّرٌ"],".) [And in anatomy, ",[1,"A cell."],"]"]},{"h":"مَا بِالدَّارِ نَافِخُ ضَرَمَةٍ","t":["[",[1,"There is not in the house a blower of a fire;"]," i. e.,] ",[1,"there is not in the house any one."]," (S.) ― -b2- ",[2,"نَافِخٌ حِضْنَيْهِ"]," [A man ",[1,"inflating,"]," or ",[1,"puffing out, his sides;"],"] ",[1,"inflated, and ready to do mischief,"]," or ",[1,"evil."]," (L, from a trad.)"]},{"h":"أَنْفَخُ","t":["A man, (S, L, K,) and a horse, (L,) ",[1,"having inflated testicles:"]," (S, L, K:) ",[1,"syn. of"],[2,"آدَرُ"],". (Mgh, in art, ",[2,"ادر"],".) ― -b2- Also, A beast of carriage ",[1,"having his pasterns inflated with wind:"]," see ",[2,"نَفِخَ"],". (L.)"]},{"h":"رَجُلٌ أُنْفُخَانٌ","t":["and ",[2,"إِنْفِخَانٌ"],", and ",[2,"أُنْفُخَانِىٌّ"],", and ",[2,"إِنْفِخَانِىٌّ"],", fem. with ",[2,"ة"],", (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"A man full of fat;"]," (K;) ",[1,"inflated with flaccid fat,"]," and so ↓ ",[2,"رحل مَنْفُوخٌ"],"; pl. ",[2,"مَنْفُوخُوَن"],". (TA.)"]},{"h":"مِنْفَخٌ","t":[": see what follows."]},{"h":"مِنْفَاخٌ","t":["(S, L, Msb, K) and ↓ ",[2,"مِنْفَخٌ"]," (Msb) The ",[1,"instrument with which a fire is blown;"]," (Msb, K:) ",[1,"a blacksmith's bellows:"]," the ",[1,"thing with which a fire"]," or ",[1,"other thing is blown:"]," (L:) the ",[1,"thing into which one blows."]," (S.) See also ",[2,"كيرٌ"]," ― -b2- ",[2,"مِنْفَاخُ الرَّاعِى"],[1,"The instrument"]," [i. e. ",[1,"reed-pipe"],"] ",[1,"of the pastor, with which he calls together the camels."]," (A, TA, voce ",[2,"شِيَاعٌ"],".)"]},{"h":"مَنَافِخُ الشَّيْطَانِ","t":["(assumed tropical:) ",[1,"The suggestions of the devil"]," (TA.)"]},{"h":"مَنْفُوخٌ","t":["(assumed tropical:) ",[1,"Big-bellied;"]," (K, TA;) [",[1,"inflated in the belly"],"]. ― -b2- Also, (K,) ↓ ",[2,"مُنْتَفِخٌ"],", (TA,) (tropical:) ",[1,"Fat;"]," as an epithet; (A, K;) [",[1,"inflated,"]," or ",[1,"swollen, with fat"],"]. See ",[2,"أُنْفِخَانٌ"],". ― -b3- ",[2,"مَنْفُوخٌ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"A coward:"]," so called because he swells out his lungs. (L.)"]},{"h":"مُنْتَفِخٌ","t":["(tropical:) A man ",[1,"inflated,"]," or ",[1,"puffed,"]," or ",[1,"filled, with pride,"]," and ",[1,"with anger."]," (L.) See ",[2,"مَنْفُوخٌ"],"."]}]},"maqayis":["النون والفاء والخاء: أصل صحيح يدل على انتفاخ وعلو. منه انتفخ الشيء انتفاخا. ويقال انتفخ النهار: علا. ونفخة الربيع: إعشابه ; لأن الأرض تربو فيه وتنتفخ. والمنفوخ: الرجل السمين. والنفخاء من الأرض مثل النبخاء ; وقد مضى."],"mufradat":["النفخ: نفخ الريح في الشيء. قال تعالى: يوم ينفخ في الصور [طه/ 102] ، ونفخ في الصور [الكهف/ 99] ، ثم نفخ فيه أخرى [الزمر/ 68] ، وذلك نحو قوله: فإذا نقر في الناقور [المدثر/ 8] ومنه نفخ الروح في النشأة الأولى، قال: ونفخت فيه من روحي [الحجر/ 29] يقال: انتفخ بطنه، ومنه استعير: انتفخ النهار: إذا ارتفع، ونفخة الربيع حين أعشب، ورجل منفوخ. أي: سمين."]}